\left[\begin{array}{cc}
0 &amp; 1\\
2 &amp; -3
\end{array}\right]
\left[\begin{array}{c}
0\\
1
\end{array}\right]
=
\left[\begin{array}{c}
1\\
-3
\end{array}\right]\] Therefore, \[Q_{c}
=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
0 &amp; 1\\
1 &amp; -3
\end{array}\right]\] \[|Q_{c}|=-1\neq0\] Hence, the system is controllable. To check observability, form the observability matrix, \[Q_{o}
=
\left[\begin{array}{c}
C\\
CA
\end{array}\right]\] First compute \(CA\), \[CA=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
1 &amp; 1
\end{array}\right]
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
0 &amp; 1\\
2 &amp; -3
\end{array}\right]
=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
2 &amp; -2
\end{array}\right]\] Therefore, \[Q_{o}
=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
1 &amp; 1\\
2 &amp; -2
\end{array}\right]\] \[|Q_{o}|=-4\neq0\] Hence, the system is observable. \[\boxed{\text{(A) Controllable and Observable.}}\]

